      ":question/id": "695b49d1-9327-503a-b244-1f7f385f59ff",
      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-14315",
      ":question/problem": "Consider the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{3{y}^{3}}{x{y}^{2}+y{x}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nIf the transformation $y=v(x)x$ is applied to the differential equation, what is the resulting equation?",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Using the transformation $y=vx$ (where $v=v(x)$), we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}+v\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(x) \\\\  & =x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}+v.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into the given differential equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{3{y}^{3}}{x{y}^{2}+y{x}^{2}} \\\\ x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}+v & =\\frac{3(vx)^{3}}{x(vx)^{2}+(vx){x}^{2}} \\\\ x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}+v & =\\frac{3{v}^{3}{x}^{3}}{v{x}^{3}(v+1)} \\\\ x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}+v & =\\frac{3{v}^{3}\\cancel{{x}^{3}}}{v\\cancel{{x}^{3}}(v+1)} \\\\ x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{3{v}^{2}}{v+1}-v \\\\ x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{3{v}^{2}}{v+1}-\\frac{v(v+1)}{v+1} \\\\ x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{3{v}^{2}-{v}^{2}-v}{v+1} \\\\ x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{2{v}^{2}-v}{v+1} \\\\ \\left(\\frac{v+1}{2{v}^{2}-v}\\right)\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{1}{x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"
    },
