      ":question/id": "b4e19450-4e51-548d-b019-a1f8398b116f",
      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-14314",
      ":question/problem": "Consider the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\left(\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{y}^{2}}\\right)+\\frac{3y}{x}.\n$$\n\nIf the transformation $y=v(x)x$ is applied to the differential equation, what is the resulting equation?",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Using the transformation $y=vx$ (where $v=v(x)$), we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}+v\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(x) \\\\  & =x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}+v.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into the given differential equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\left(\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{y}^{2}}\\right)+\\frac{3y}{x} \\\\ x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}+v & =\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\left(\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{v}^{2}{x}^{2}}\\right)+\\frac{3vx}{x} \\\\ x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}+v & =\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\left(\\frac{1}{{v}^{2}}\\right)+3v \\\\ x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x} & =\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\left(\\frac{1}{{v}^{2}}\\right)+2v \\\\ \\left(\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\left(\\frac{1}{{v}^{2}}\\right)+2v}\\right)\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{1}{x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"
    },
