      ":question/id": "647415db-3b65-5b2e-8b3d-f70381af49e3",
      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-90601",
      ":question/problem": "Consider the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{y}{x}-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(\\frac{y}{x}\\right).\n$$\n\nIf the transformation $y=v(x)x$ is applied to the differential equation, what is the resulting equation?",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Using the transformation $y=vx$ (where $v=v(x)$), we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}+v\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(x) \\\\  & =x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}+v.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into the given differential equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{y}{x}-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(\\frac{y}{x}\\right) \\\\ x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}+v & =\\frac{vx}{x}-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(\\frac{vx}{x}\\right) \\\\ x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}+v & =v-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡v \\\\ x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x} & =-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡v \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡v}\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x} & =-\\frac{2}{x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"
    },
